.TH BPFAGENT 1 "August 2026" "bpfagent 0.1.0" "User Manual"

.SH NAME
bpfagent \- EBPF program manager and Prometheus metrics extractor

.SH SYNOPSIS
.B bpfagent
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B bpfagent
is a daemon that loads eBPF programs and exposes their metrics to Prometheus.
It provides a modular architecture for running multiple eBPF programs and
exporting statistics via an HTTP-based metrics endpoint.

.SH eBPF PROGRAMS

The following eBPF programs are supported:

.TP
.B kfree_skb
Traces packet drops at the kernel's \fIkfree_skb\fR tracepoint. Counts drops by
reason (e.g., TCP_CSUM, NO_SOCKET, QDISC_DROP, etc.) and displays drop
statistics.

.TP
.B sca
Traces socket communication latency per process. Measures latency based on
socket path + direction (TO/FROM) matching, tracking moving average latency
per process name (2-second sliding window).

.TP
.B irss
Measures UDP-to-raw-IP forwarding latency. On UDP receive (port-filtered
kprobe): stores timestamp keyed by the first 4 payload bytes. On raw-IP send
to the configured destination: matches the key, removes it, accumulates
latency.

.SH OPTIONS

.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-daemon
Run in daemon mode (background, no stdout output). The process detaches from
the controlling terminal and runs in the background.

.TP
.BR \-i ", " \-\-metrics\-ip \fIADDRESS\fR
Set the metrics server IP address. Default: 0.0.0.0 (all interfaces).

.TP
.BR \-p ", " \-\-metrics\-port \fIPORT\fR
Set the metrics server port. Default: 9101.

.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-verbose
Enable verbose output. This overrides daemon mode and outputs to stdout for
interactive debugging.

.TP
.BR \-f ", " \-\-config\-file \fIPATH\fR
Path to configuration file. If not specified, the following default paths are
searched:
.IP
/etc/bpfagent.conf
.br
/etc/bpfagent/bpfagent.conf
.br
/usr/local/etc/bpfagent.conf
.br
/usr/local/etc/bpfagent/bpfagent.conf
.br
~/.bpfagent.conf (if HOME is set)
.br
~/.config/bpfagent/config.toml (if HOME is set)
.br
./bpfagent.conf (current directory for development)

.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Display help information.

.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Display version information.

.SH CONFIGURATION FILE

The configuration file uses TOML format and controls daemon settings and eBPF
program loading:

.EX
# Daemon settings
pid_file = "/tmp/bpfagent.pid"
working_directory = "/"
log_file = "/tmp/bpfagent.log"

# EBPF programs to load and run
[[ebpf_programs]]
name = "kfree_skb"
enabled = true

[[ebpf_programs]]
name = "sca"
enabled = true

[[ebpf_programs]]
name = "irss"
enabled = true

# Optional program-specific settings
[ebpf_programs.settings]
listen_port = 5020        # IRSS UDP listen port (CRYPTO side)
raw_dest = "10.10.10.253" # IRSS raw-IP destination (MAC)
.EE

.SH METRICS ENDPOINT

The metrics server listens on the configured IP and port (default 0.0.0.0:9101)
and exposes metrics in Prometheus format at the /metrics path.

Example access:
.IP
curl http://localhost:9101/metrics

.SH PROMETHEUS CONFIGURATION

Add the following to your Prometheus \fIscrape_configs\fR:

.EX
scrape_configs:
  - job_name: 'bpfagent'
    static_configs:
      - targets: ['localhost:9101']
.EE

.SH PREREQUISITES

.IP \(bu 2
Linux kernel 5.8+ with BPF support

.IP \(bu 2
Rust and Cargo

.IP \(bu 2
bpf-linker: \fBcargo install bpf-linker\fR

.IP \(bu 2
BPF tracepoint support for the enabled programs:
.RS
.IP \(bu 2
skb:kfree_skb (for kfree_skb program)
.IP \(bu 2
syscalls:sys_enter_sendmsg, syscalls:sys_exit_recvmsg (for SCA and IRSS programs)
.IP \(bu 2
kprobe support for udp_recvmsg (for IRSS program)
.RE

.IP \(bu 2
BTF debug info (CONFIG_DEBUG_INFO_BTF=y) recommended for best compatibility

.SH EXAMPLES

.TP
Run in interactive mode (default):
.IP
sudo bpfagent

.TP
Run in daemon mode:
.IP
sudo bpfagent -d

.TP
Run with custom config file:
.IP
sudo bpfagent -f /etc/bpfagent.conf

.TP
Run in verbose mode (overrides daemon mode):
.IP
sudo bpfagent -v

.TP
Listen on localhost only with custom port:
.IP
sudo bpfagent -i 127.0.0.1 -p 9999

.SH FILES

.TP
.B /etc/bpfagent.conf
Default system-wide configuration file location.

.TP
.B /tmp/bpfagent.pid
Default location for the PID file when running as a daemon.

.TP
.B /tmp/bpfagent.log
Default location for the log file when running as a daemon.

.SH EXIT STATUS

.TP
.B 0
Success.

.TP
.B 1
Error (e.g., failed to load eBPF programs, invalid configuration, permission denied).

